<!-- SIP Formula -->
<div class="mt-8">
    <h2 id="sip-calculator-formula" class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>📐</span>
        <span>SIP Calculator Formula</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="bg-slate-50 p-5 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm overflow-x-auto shadow-xs">
        <p class="font-bold text-emerald-800 mb-2 font-sans">Future Value of SIP (Annuity Due):</p>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 bg-white p-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-200/80">FV = P × [ { (1 + i)<sup>n</sup> - 1 } / i ] × (1 + i)</p>
        <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 font-sans">
            <div>
                <dt class="inline font-bold text-slate-900">FV</dt>
                <dd class="inline">= Future Value (Maturity Amount)</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt class="inline font-bold text-slate-900">P</dt>
                <dd class="inline">= Monthly Investment Amount</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt class="inline font-bold text-slate-900">i</dt>
                <dd class="inline">= Monthly Rate (Annual Rate ÷ 12 ÷ 100)</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
                <dt class="inline font-bold text-slate-900">n</dt>
                <dd class="inline">= Total Payments (Years × 12)</dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Our calculator uses month-by-month simulation with annual step-up compounding and lumpsum starting points, providing higher precision than simple closed-form approximations.</p>
</div>
